<p>I made sure Google could actually find and index my content by submitting a sitemap. A dynamic sitemap — like the one built into this site — updates automatically as you publish. Connecting to Google Search Console took only a few minutes, and it let me confirm pages were being crawled instead of guessing. Indexing matters because AdSense needs to evaluate real, discoverable pages, not an empty shell. Once submitted, I watched the coverage report to make sure every post was indexed before I hit apply.</p>
<h2>5. Met AdSense Program Policies</h2>
<p>Before applying, I reviewed Google’s policies and double-checked that my content was not in any restricted category. I also confirmed my privacy policy, cookie notice, and overall experience lined up with what Google expects from trustworthy websites. Things like misleading claims, copyright infringement, or clickbait will sink an application fast. I removed anything borderline and made sure my disclosures were honest and easy to find.</p>
