        'content' => '<p>Your email list is an asset you own. Social algorithms change; your list does not. Here is how to turn subscribers into buyers without burning them out or ending up in spam.</p>
<h2>Offer a Lead Magnet</h2>
<p>Give people a reason to subscribe: a checklist, mini-course, or template. The better the bribe, the better the list. Make it specific — “10 Meal Plans Under $30” beats “Free Cooking Guide” because specificity promises immediate value and attracts the right reader.</p>
<h2>Send a Welcome Sequence</h2>
<p>New subscribers get three to five emails that deliver value, share your story, and introduce your best offer naturally. This is where most first sales happen, so write it with care. The welcome sequence sets the tone for the entire relationship and frames you as helpful before you ever ask for money.</p>
<h2>Nurture With Value</h2>
<p>Most emails should teach or entertain. Pitch occasionally, not constantly. Trust earns the click; constant selling earns the unsubscribe. A good ratio early on is roughly four value emails for every one pitch, shifting slightly as the relationship matures.</p>
